IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `it-types`

-- Income Tax Act 2007, personal income tax — GOAL 2: TAXABLE INCOME AND
-- LIABILITY.
--
--   "What are the person's annual gross income, net income, taxable income
--    and income tax liability for the tax year?"
--
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/act_public_2007_97.txt — ss BC 1-BC 7,
-- Schedule 1, part A, clause 1.

§ `Goal 2 — taxable income and liability`

-- BC 2 "A person's annual gross income for a tax year is the total of their
-- assessable income that is allocated to the corresponding income year."
@ref s BC 2
GIVEN y IS A `Tax year facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the annual gross income for` y MEANS y's `assessable income allocated to the year`

-- BC 4 "(1) If ... annual gross income is more than their annual total
-- deduction, the difference is their net income ... (2) ... equals ...,
-- their net income for the year is zero. (3) If ... annual total deduction is
-- more than their annual gross income, the difference is their net loss ...,
-- and their net income for the year is zero."
@ref ss BC 3, BC 4
GIVEN y IS A `Tax year facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the net income for` y MEANS
    max 0 (`the annual gross income for` y MINUS y's `deductions allocated to the year`)

@ref ss BC 3, BC 4(3)
GIVEN y IS A `Tax year facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the net loss for` y MEANS
    max 0 (y's `deductions allocated to the year` MINUS `the annual gross income for` y)

-- BC 5 "A person's taxable income for a tax year is determined by
-- subtracting any available tax loss that the person has from their net
-- income under Part I". Part I subtracts a loss only up to the net income.
@ref s BC 5
GIVEN y IS A `Tax year facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the taxable income for` y MEANS
    max 0 (`the net income for` y MINUS y's `tax loss available to subtract`)

-- Schedule 1, part A, clause 1: "tax under table 1 means the total tax,
-- calculated for each dollar in the person's taxable income, using table 1:
-- taxable income means the number of dollars in the person's taxable income.
-- ... Find the range in the second column for each dollar in the person's
-- taxable income, and apply the relevant rate for the dollar in the third
-- column." Only whole dollars are taxed (fork F1); the bands are an input,
-- in order.
@ref Schedule 1, part A, cl 1
GIVEN income IS A NUMBER
      bands IS A LIST OF Band
      lower IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the tax under table 1 on` income `, bands` bands `, above` lower MEANS
    CONSIDER bands
    WHEN EMPTY THEN 0
    WHEN b FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        CONSIDER b's `band ends at`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN max 0 (dollars MINUS lower) TIMES b's `rate for each dollar in the band`
        WHEN JUST top THEN
                max 0 (min dollars top MINUS lower) TIMES b's `rate for each dollar in the band`
            PLUS `the tax under table 1 on` income `, bands` rest `, above` top
    WHERE
        dollars MEANS FLOOR income

@ref Schedule 1, part A, cl 1
@export The income tax on a natural person's taxable income under Schedule 1, part A, clause 1 of the Income Tax Act 2007 (NZ): each whole dollar taxed at the rate for its band in table 1 (the bands are an input, since the table is lost in the converted text). DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN income IS A NUMBER  @desc The taxable income
      bands IS A LIST OF Band  @desc Table 1: each band's top (none for the last) and rate, in order
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the tax under table 1 on` income `, bands` bands MEANS
    `the tax under table 1 on` income `, bands` bands `, above` 0

-- BC 1 "(1) The income tax liability of a non-filing taxpayer for a tax year
-- is the total tax withheld from amounts of income included in the
-- taxpayer's annual gross income for the year. (2) The income tax liability
-- of a filing taxpayer ... is calculated under sections BC 2 to BC 6." BC 6
-- "(1) ... multiplying their taxable income for the tax year by the basic
-- tax rate ... (2) If the income tax liability calculated under subsection
-- (1) is zero or negative, ... [it] is zero." BC 7 "(1) The income tax
-- liability for a tax year of a person who has schedular income ... is the
-- total of— (a) their schedular income tax liability ...; and (b) the amount
-- that would be their income tax liability for the year if they had no
-- schedular income."
@ref ss BC 1, BC 6, BC 7(1)
@export A natural person's income tax liability for a tax year under ss BC 1-BC 7 of the Income Tax Act 2007 (NZ): for a non-filing taxpayer, the tax withheld; for a filing taxpayer, the Schedule 1 tax on their taxable income (net income less any available tax loss), never below zero, plus — with schedular income — the schedular income tax liability, the rest of the income being taxed as if there were no schedular income. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN y IS A `Tax year facts`  @desc Filing status, tax withheld, assessable income, deductions, available tax loss, schedular income and its liability, and table 1
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the income tax liability for` y MEANS
    IF   NOT y's `a filing taxpayer`
    THEN y's `total tax withheld from income in annual gross income`
    ELSE max 0 (`the tax under table 1 on` ordinary `, bands` (y's `table 1`)) PLUS schedular
    WHERE
        schedular MEANS IF y's `schedular income` GREATER THAN 0 THEN y's `schedular income tax liability` ELSE 0
        ordinary MEANS max 0 (`the taxable income for` y MINUS y's `schedular income`)
